<title>INDIA: Indian Hotels 1996/97 net seen better.</title>
<headline>Indian Hotels 1996/97 net seen better.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Net profit of Indian Hotels, the owners of Taj hotel chain, is expected to improve 15.63 percent to 1.6 billion rupees in the year ended March 31, 1997, a Reuter poll of 28 leading securities and brokerage firms said.</p>
<p>Analysts forecast a high of 1.88 billion rupees and a low of 1.34 billion rupees against 1.40 billion a year ago.</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>INDIAN HOTELS  ----PAT seen up 15.63%, sales 12.04%</p>
<p>		     Net profit   1995/96    Net sales   1995/96</p>
<p>				(in million rupees)</p>
<p>Average		1,625.47  1,405.70     6,132.84    5,473.60</p>
<p>High		   1,883.60		   6,750.00</p>
<p>Low		    1,343.00		   5,551.00</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
